  "label": "General adult audience familiar with domestic humor and gender role stereotypes",
  "description": "The meme targets a broad adult audience who can relate to the relatable, exaggerated suffering of cutting onions while trying to suppress tears in front of one's wife. It relies on shared cultural knowledge of the biological reaction to onions and the social expectation for men to suppress emotional displays, particularly in domestic settings. The humor is lighthearted and non-toxic, appealing to those who appreciate everyday domestic mishaps and gendered stereotypes in a comedic context.",
